  "result": "Excellent! The VAT feature is working perfectly. The calculation shows:\n- **Subtotal**: \u20ac1,487.00 (sum of all line totals before discount)\n- **Discount**: \u20ac74.35 (5% gold tier discount applied across all lines)\n- **VAT**: \u20ac172.74 (calculated per line on amount after discount, then summed)\n  - Line 1 (DES-HOUR, 21%): (\u20ac850 - \u20ac42.50) \u00d7 21% = \u20ac169.58\n  - Line 2 (PRINT-A4, 9%): (\u20ac37 - \u20ac1.85) \u00d7 9% = \u20ac3.16\n  - Line 3 (WORKSHOP, 0% exempt): \u20ac0\n- **Total**: \u20ac1,585.39 (subtotal - discount + vat)\n\nThe render output shows the breakdown with Subtotal, Discount, and VAT all displayed above the Total.\n\n## Summary of VAT Implementation\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/invoices.js**: Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n   - Calculate VAT per line on the amount after discount\n   - Round each line's VAT individually\n   - Return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - Total formula: `subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n\n2. **src/render.js**: Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to:\n   - Show Subtotal line when discount > 0\n   - Show Discount line when discount > 0  \n   - Show VAT line when vat > 0\n   - All amounts formatted through `formatEuros()`\n\n3. **Tests**: \n   - Updated 10 existing tests to expect VAT field\n   - Added 12 comprehensive VAT tests covering:\n     - Different VAT rates (0, 9, 21)\n     - VAT calculation on amount after discount\n     - Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n     - VAT rounded per line\n     - VAT display in rendered invoices\n\n**Test results:** All 126 tests passing \u2713",
